---
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '@/components/SectionHeading.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="About" description="Background, education and how I work.">
  <section class="section-block">
    <SectionHeading
      title="About"
      subtitle="A career of production systems, now pointed at frontier AI."
    />
    <div class="mt-8 surface p-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I'm Isabelle De Backer, a senior software engineer and technical lead based in Sydney. I've spent my career
          building payments and data infrastructure at scale — core banking across Europe, digital platforms at
          Commonwealth Bank, and the HICAPS claiming platform at NAB, where I led a 7-engineer team on a system
          processing 3,000 claims/hour across 97,000 providers.
        </p>
        <p>
          From 2024 to 2026 I was a founding engineer at an AI startup, building a real-time conversational voice
          agent with live screen-share from scratch, and co-designing a distributed pipeline that surfaced
          permission-security findings across enterprise knowledge bases. I also contributed features and refactors
          to a permission-aware RAG engine. I work across the full stack — Python, TypeScript, Svelte and React, on
          GCP and AWS — and I own delivery end to end: discovery, system design, build, production rollout, and
          on-call.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've been on both sides of delivery — engineer and delivery manager — so I'm comfortable scoping ambiguous
          problems with stakeholders, making trade-offs between scope, speed and quality, and staying calm when
          production is on fire. I hold a Master of Complex Systems (University of Sydney, 2023, High Distinction —
          research in network synchronisation, information theory and nonlinear dynamics) and a Master's in
          Electronics Engineering (Free University of Brussels, 1997).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
